      "nets": ["+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "C1 is a 100nF capacitor connected between the +5V rail (LM1117-5.0 output) and GND.",
      "expected": "The LM1117-5.0 requires a 10uF output capacitor for stability; 100nF is far too small and may cause oscillation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"100nF\") (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U2\") (value \"LM1117-5.0\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"1\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"VO\") ..."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The 5V regulator may be unstable or oscillate, causing unreliable operation of the ATtiny microcontrollers and other 5V logic.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a likely anomaly: C1, the output capacitor for the LM1117-5.0 regulator, is 100nF instead of the required 10uF, which can make the 5V rail unstable."
}

